# Normalize EOL for all files that Git considers text files.
* text=auto eol=lf

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Release packaging.
#
# `git archive` builds the distributable .zip from these rules, so this file is
# the single source of truth for what ships to both the Godot Asset Store and
# the Godot Asset Library. Everything is excluded by default and re-enabled
# explicitly below - a denylist would silently ship new root files.
#
# Anything shipped at the project root lands directly in the user's project and
# will overwrite a file of the same name, so add root entries with care.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

/**                     export-ignore

# The plugin itself.
/addons                 !export-ignore
/addons/**              !export-ignore

# Sample project. Users can skip this folder when importing from the Asset Store.
/forge_samples          !export-ignore
/forge_samples/**       !export-ignore

# Auto-imported by MSBuild, so installing the plugin needs no .csproj edits.
/Directory.Build.props  !export-ignore

# Deliberately NOT shipped:
#
#   forge_tags.tres      This repository's own tag source. Tag sources belong to the user and one is
#                        created on demand when the plugin is enabled. Shipping ours would overwrite
#                        their tags on every install and update. The sample tags ship separately, in
#                        forge_samples/forge_samples_tags.tres, to be added as a source of its own.
#   Forge.Dev.props      Analyzers and style rules for developing this repository.
#   Forge Godot.csproj   This repository's own Godot project files - they would overwrite the user's.
#   Forge Godot.sln
#   project.godot
#   export_presets.cfg
#   icon.svg / icon.png
#   README.md            The plugin's own README ships as addons/forge/README.md.
#   LICENSE              Ships as addons/forge/LICENSE, so it cannot overwrite the user's LICENSE.
#   docs/                Published on GitHub.
